   "id": 646095,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol start=\"11\">\n<li>Tyler and Han are trying to solve this system by substitution:</li>\n</ol>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\left\\{\\begin{array}{l}x+3y=-5\\\\9x+3y=3\\end{array}\\right.\">\\left\\{\\begin{array}{l}x+3y=-5\\\\9x+3y=3\\end{array}\\right.</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>Tyler's first step is to isolate x in the first equation to get <span data-math=\"x = -5 - 3y.\">x = -5 - 3y.</span></p></li>\n<li><p>Han's first step is to isolate 3y in the first equation to get <span data-math=\"3y = -5 - x.\">3y = -5 - x.</span></p></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Solve using both methods to show that both first steps can be used to solve the system and will yield the same solution.</p>\n<p>What is the solution to the system?</p>\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1271630,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"(-5,0)\">(-5,0)</span>"
    },
    {
     "id": 1271631,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"(4,-3)\">(4,-3)</span>"
    },
    {
     "id": 1271632,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"(0,1)\">(0,1)</span>"
    },
    {
     "id": 1271633,
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"(1,-2)\">(1,-2)</span>"
    }
   ],
